# 19. Key Concepts Demonstrated

This laboratory demonstrates the following concepts:

- Forward Kinematics
- Robot coordinate frames
- Joint-space and Cartesian-space representation
- Rotation matrices
- Homogeneous transformation matrices
- Denavit-Hartenberg parameters
- Serial kinematic chains
- Numerical matrix multiplication
- End-effector pose calculation
- Robotics Toolbox
- MuJoCo simulation
- Real-time robot visualization
- Cartesian position tracking
- Kinematic validation

---

# 20. Conclusion

This laboratory provides a complete workflow for understanding and implementing forward kinematics for robotic manipulators.

The mathematical formulation is first established using planar trigonometric relationships and homogeneous transformation matrices. These formulations are then implemented numerically using Python and NumPy and independently verified using Robotics Toolbox.

The implementation is further integrated with MuJoCo to provide an interactive physics-based simulation of 6-DOF and 7-DOF robotic manipulators.

By changing the joint variables and observing the resulting end-effector position, the relationship between joint-space motion and Cartesian-space motion can be studied and validated in real time.

